  <fragment slot="bio">
    Sofiya V codes, deejays, and produces various events in New York City.
  </fragment>

  <fragment slot="inkblot response">
    I see:
    <br /><br />two saxophone players (sound bubbles emerging from the
    instruments),
    <br /><br />two E.T.s smoking bongs
    <br /><br />embryos
  </fragment>

  <fragment slot="dream log">
    When I emerge from whatever state of unawareness I was in, I see that I am
    at some kind of sinister discotheque. [[[physical description here]]] I feel
    relief when I recognize some acquaintances in the crowd of partygoers. But
    when I rest my gaze on any one person's features, they contort into
    something strange and unfriendly.

    <br /><br />It's hard to get oriented in my nauseous state. The room is big
    and then it’s small until it’s big again. No one knows me here. They are
    dancing automatons whose source of movement is unclear. I am the only one
    standing still. The taste of metal blooms unpleasantly in my mouth.

    <br /><br />Eventually my unease briefly gives way to a rapturous glimmer.
    There is something beautiful in the danger of this gathering, glowing and
    radioactive.

    <br /><br /> I soon find out why the automatons dance. Whatever compels them takes
    me in as well, but only somatically. Whatever remains of my spirit is small and
    impotent, but aware, within my body. The source of my own movement is unclear
    and relentless.

    <br /><br /> After an undeterminable period of time, the sun rises. I only know
    this because [[[reference to physical space]]]. The center of the dance floor
    collapses and everything in sight succumbs to the whirlpool. Lasers bend impossibly
    towards the newly formed void. The ethereal haze that filled the room earlier
    is now a dense river rushing past us. My chest cannot expand against the bassline,
    and the light flares in my vision multiply and expand until I cannot see at all.

    <br /><br /> I am in my apartment and it's Sunday afternoon. Despite the pleasant
    weather and an empty to-do list, I am disturbed by an ambient sense of doom and
    a metallic echo in my mouth.
  </fragment>

  <fragment slot="caption">
    New York on 35mm by <a href="https://eamonbonner.darkroom.com"
      >Eamon Bonner</a
    >
  </fragment>
